Z||000005||cardealer||08-18-2001||09:49 PM||||i had a vega with a 327 when i was a teenager and they just look old.<P>archie two words on the wagon.. aaahhh,,NO <BR> <BR>i had a 944 (4 banger) loved that car, but finding one with a bad motor and affordable for a conversion and a kit(?)is going to be a pita. jag's kinda a combination between a vega and 944, old and hard to find a good enough deal.<P>it looks like a s10 blazer is the one. found a real nice one with a blown motor for $750.00. a swap kit from jegs including headers is less than $200.00!<BR>thanks for all the suggestions !<BR>tony ||||reg||6
Z||000006||rockcrawl||08-18-2001||10:07 PM||||I did a 350 TBI/700R4 swap into a friends 4x4 s-10 Blazer. It was pertty cool. It would roast the 31" tires no problem. But you're right, there are lots of V8 S10s running around. How about an old Opel Manta GT. There's one for sale down the road from me and it's got me thinking. I need to stop and see the asking price. That's a car I rarely see around here and IMO it's not a bad looking car. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Archie||08-18-2001||10:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>old Opel Manta GT.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Are you talking about a Opel Manta or a Opel GT.  (4 seats or 2 seats?)<P>I did a V-8 swap into an Opel GT about 24 years ago. It was fast in a straight line, but like my V-8 powered 240Z (about 22 years ago) the unitized chassis twisted like mad.<P>HEHE, reminds me of a story.... on the Z car, the engine was making so much torque that I could break the windshield on demand by using only the gas pedal.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000008||Archie||08-18-2001||10:29 PM||||P.S. You know you're getting old, when everything reminds you of a story.<P>Archie||||reg||1
