Z||000013||Dan86gt3.8||08-20-2001||01:35 AM||||So archie you have done v8 240 z's also?  <P>Whats better in your opinion a v8 z Or a v8 fiero?<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000014||Archie||08-20-2001||08:29 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dan86gt3.8:<BR><B>So archie you have done v8 240 z's also?  <P>Whats better in your opinion a v8 z Or a v8 fiero?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Before I put a SBC into a Fiero, I had spent more than 15 years putting big engines into small cars. I was always looking for the ideal sports car. It needed to have V-8 power & torque, 2 seats & good handling. I've put V-8 Chevy engines into (among others) a Bug Eyed Sprite, Spitfire, XKE, Opel GT, Z car, Vega, S-10 & finally a Fiero. <P>Most of them had poor handling when I finished them. Too much front end weight or frame twist or cooling problems (remember this was back when no-one made an electric radiator fan).<P>I never built more than one until I got to the Fiero. IMHO, for the purpose I intended, the Fiero was better than all the others.<P>Archie||||reg||1
